    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver — here is what is settled and what is not, and why this case goes to a human reviewer instead of being paid out or dismissed today.\n\nWhat is settled. The platform's optimal route between Paya Lebar Square and Tampines MRT is 9.4 km and 14.0 minutes. The GPS trace for the trip records 23.86 km — the trace figure governs over the trip record's rounded 23.9 km under POL-RD-01 — an excess of 14.46 km, or 153.83% of optimal. That clears both establishment tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km absolute) and is a material deviation on this trip's own evidence. The trace is clean for policy purposes: 100% coverage, 229 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gaps and no jumps, so no independent corroboration is required under POL-RD-07. The rider has discharged the POL-RD-08 burden: the trip record, trace and fare breakdown all carry TRP-00504, her profile's deviation_claims_60d is 0, and no extra corroboration is demanded of her. The fare is METERED, and on the fare breakdown's own constants the optimal-route fare would be 3.80 + (0.75 x 9.4) + (0.28 x 14.0) = 15.57 at the 1.0 surge multiplier recorded on that artifact, plus the 0.80 platform fee. Against the 33.17 charged, that is a refund of 17.60 — 53.06% of the charge, above the 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% that would convert it to a full refund. Nothing is added for pass-throughs: ERP, tolls, surcharge, waiting fee and promo are all nil, so POL-RD-09 contributes nothing further. There was no rider-requested detour (the chat log exists and is empty, so POL-RD-04 cannot run), no amended pickup or dropoff (POL-RD-05 cannot run), the vehicle was RYDE_X so POL-RD-12 does not apply, and the fare was not upfront-quoted so POL-RD-11 does not apply. I have also run the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check that materiality requires: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed trips, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift is available and no conduct referral follows. Only those two profile fields were used for that test; the lifetime counters such as prior_deviation_flags are context only and grounded no finding.\n\nWhat is not settled. The driver's explanation is that a car behind him flashed high beams several times near the exit, that he believed an accident lay ahead so he stayed on the expressway, and that he turned back at the next exit — in the rider's account, he said he thought the road was closed. That is an external-event defence, and the only clause that can carry it is POL-RD-03, which requires a traffic_advisory naming the affected segment with a validity window overlapping the trip. The only advisory artifact in the pool, EV-ADVIS-00504-01, is MISSING: it has no payload, its issue code is MISSING_ARTIFACT and its admissibility weight_multiplier is 0.0, so it can carry no fact and only its absence is citable (POL-GEN-02(3)). POL-RD-10(5) names precisely this situation — a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory — as one in which no final monetary ruling may issue. The driver's account on its own does not establish a closure: a stated reason records only that it was stated, a record the platform generates is the platform's, and POL-RD-03 reads the advisory rather than the driver's belief, so a general assertion of this kind does not discharge his POL-RD-08 burden. But the absent advisory is a gap in the record, not a finding against him, and the same principle that stops a data failure being turned into a finding for one side stops it being turned into a finding for the other.\n\nResult. The outcome is ESCALATE, which is terminal: no money moves now, both money fields are null, and the disputed 33.17 is held rather than collected or refunded. The rider's arithmetic is not rejected — if the reviewer concludes there was no closure, the POL-RD-02 refund of 17.60 is the figure that follows; if the reviewer concludes the driver's external-event account is made out on a properly produced advisory, exoneration under POL-RD-03 would change that. What would resolve the case is the LTA advisory record for the Paya Lebar–Tampines corridor on the evening of 23 August 2026, or a record confirming that no advisory was issued. My confidence is 0.70, at the platform floor."
