    "explanation": "Both of you should know why this case is not being decided today.\n\nWhat the record shows clearly. The trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown all describe trip TRP-00504, and the trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 229 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, an empty gaps array and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. On that trace the vehicle ran 23.86 km against the platform's 9.4 km optimal route — an excess of 14.46 km, or 153.83% of optimal — which is a material deviation under POL-RD-01. The rider is right about that. The rider is also right that nothing on the face of the record excuses the detour: the chat log is complete and empty (0 messages, matching the trip record's chat_message_count of 0), so there is no rider-requested detour for POL-RD-04 to run on, and the trip record shows pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at both null, so POL-RD-05 has no re-quote to apply. The trace is clean under POL-RD-07, so no independent corroboration of the excess is required, and the rider's profile carries no deviation_claims_60d history that would demand more.\n\nWhere the case cannot be decided. The driver's explanation is an external-event defence — a car flashed its high beams behind him, he believed an accident lay ahead, so he stayed on the expressway and turned back at the next exit. On this policy that defence can only run through POL-RD-03, which requires a traffic advisory naming the affected road or segment with a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have been there. The only advisory artifact for this corridor, EV-ADVIS-00504-01, is absent: its admissibility status is MISSING, the blocking issue MISSING_ARTIFACT fired, it has no payload, its weight multiplier is 0.0, and its detail records that no advisory covers the PIE eastbound between Paya Lebar and Tampines in this window. Under POL-GEN-02 a missing artifact carries no fact and supports neither side, and its absence is itself citable. POL-RD-10(5) names this precise situation — a closure asserted with no traffic advisory — and directs that no final ruling issue on an empty record. That is terminal: the disputed SGD 33.17 is held rather than collected or refunded, and no driver compensation is paid. The human reviewer should receive the case summary, both advocate briefs and the admissibility report, and the question to resolve is whether any traffic advisory covered that corridor and window, or whether an independent source (a chat admission, the charged ERP gantries, or a platform-derived distance) corroborates the driver's account.\n\nWhat the money would have been. Had the defence been testable, the refund would have been arithmetic, not discretionary. The trip is METERED, so POL-RD-02 applies: (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 9.4 km + 0.28 x 14.0 min) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from the fare breakdown + 0.80 platform fee = 15.57 recomputed fare. Against charged_total of 33.17 that is a 17.60 refund, 53.06% of the charge — above the 0.50 de minimis floor, so a refund would issue, and below the 90% share that would convert it into a full refund. Nothing is added on top for ERP, tolls, surcharge or waiting time: erp_gantries is empty and erp_lines, tolls_erp, airport_surcharge and waiting_time_fee are all 0.00, and POL-RD-09(1) would in any event forbid counting off-route ERP twice. Both advocates' arithmetic on this point is accepted; because the escalation displaces the ruling, neither the 17.60 refund nor the 33.17 charge moves today.\n\nPoints both sides agree on, and so do I. No POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation pattern is established: the driver's trailing-90-day deviation flags are 0 against 250 completed trips in the same window, so neither limb of the test is met, the FULL_REFUND uplift is unavailable and no driver-conduct referral follows. POL-GEN-01 confines deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d to that single test, and no other profile entry — the driver's rating, lifetime trips or lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter, or anything on the rider's profile — grounded any part of this decision. The vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 has no application.\n\nConfidence. The cap is the evidence the ruling actually rests on. This ruling rests on the record's inability to test the driver's defence, and the only artifact touching that question, EV-ADVIS-00504-01, is absent at weight 0.0 and can carry no fact, while the rider's underlying measurements all sit on artifacts at weight 1.0. I therefore report 0.60, below the platform's 0.70 floor, which independently requires escalation under POL-RD-10(1) as well as under POL-RD-10(5)."
